Added `signer-manager-v2.clar`, a revision of the reference signer-manager contract. Unused sBTC withdrawal fee budget (`max-fee - actual-fee`) from an accepted withdrawal is now credited back to the staker who earned it via `settle-accepted-withdrawal` / `claim-refund`, instead of pooling for an admin sweep. Stakers set a `min-claim` floor so a third party cannot force an L1 payout that burns their reward on Bitcoin fees, and can now set or clear their payout config directly on the contract rather than re-driving `stake` / `stake-update` on pox-5. Fee increases are queued and only take effect two reward cycles later, giving stakers time to unstake; decreases still apply immediately. L1 payouts are checked against the sBTC dust limit up front, so a claim that cannot succeed fails with `ERR_BELOW_DUST_LIMIT` rather than an opaque error from the sBTC contracts. Unclaimed rewards are tracked per `(reward-cycle, bond-index)` so a claim against one cycle cannot be funded from another cycle's reserve, and the per-cycle rounding residue stays reserved in the contract with no path for an admin to reach it. The last admin can no longer be removed.
